 "// note": "Waterfalls and rivers that end at a cliff. Land-to-land (row 8, columns 5-13): lifted plains with a wall on their south-west and south-east edges down to grass; a river runs down the edge between 9,8 and 10,8, falls over the south-east face of 9,8, and continues on the low ground along the east edges of 8,9 and 8,10. Land-to-ocean (row 16): the same wall facing a coast strip; the river runs down the edge between 9,16 and 10,16 and pours over the south-east face of 9,16 into the sea, where it ends. Dead ends (rows 7 and 8, columns 17-25, two tiles deep, walled on the north too except where the river rises behind 18,7): a river on the plateau runs from the back of 18,7 down its east edge, along the north-east edge of 19,8 and down the edge between 19,8 and 20,8, and stops at the brink with nothing below it; a river on the low ground starts at the foot of the wall, under 23,8, and runs down the east edges of 22,9 and 22,10.",
